# WN22-SO-000200: Windows Server 2022 setting Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (if client agrees) must be configured to Enabled.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000200-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 setting Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (if client agrees) must be configured to Enabled.`
    description `The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. Digitally signed SMB packets aid in preventing man-in-the-middle attacks. If this policy is enabled, the SMB server will negotiate SMB packet signing as requested by the client. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-afr-ads,ksi-cna-mat,ksi-cna-uln,ksi-svc-snt`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI:KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI:KSI-CNA-ULN,KSI:KSI-SVC-SNT,NIST-800-53:SC-8,NIST-800-53:SC-8(1)`
    control_objective `KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI-CNA-ULN,KSI-SVC-SNT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (if client agrees) to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_AFR_ADS `Windows Server implements KSI-AFR-ADS by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CNA_MAT `Windows Server implements KSI-CNA-MAT by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CNA_ULN `Windows Server implements KSI-CNA-ULN by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_SNT `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-SNT by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_SC_8 `Windows Server implements SC-8 by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_SC_8_1 `Windows Server implements SC-8(1) by setting registry value 'EnableSecuritySignature' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanManServer\Parameters`
        name `EnableSecuritySignature`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
